// ── Using this template ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. Rename to SERIAL_CRC.pnach, e.g. SLUS-12345_DEADBEEF.pnach. Serial and
//    CRC: right-click the game in PCSX2 -> Properties -> Summary.
// 2. Fill in the groups you need and delete the rest.
// 3. Delete this entire comment block. Format reference: docs/pnach-format.md
//
// ── Rule: a finished .pnach contains no // comments ─────────────────────
// Ship these keys and nothing else: gametitle=, [Group], author=,
// description=, gsinterlacemode=, patch=. No header block, no per-address
// annotations, no "same builder, NTSC path" notes next to a patch= line.
//
// This is not a style preference — it is a question of which file the
// writing belongs in:
//
//   description=                 one or two sentences the user actually
//                                reads in PCSX2's Patches tab. Say what the
//                                patch does and what it costs.
//   the devlog                   addresses, disassembly, why each value,
//                                what was tried and ruled out. It lives in
//                                docs/<category>/devlog-SERIAL-slug.md,
//                                where <category> is deinterlace, deblur,
//                                60fps or misc.
//
// If you are about to explain an address, you are writing the devlog. Put it
// there. A pnach carrying that explanation has it in the wrong file, and the
// next person to read the patch has to scroll past it to find the six lines
// that matter.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gametitle=Game Title (NTSC-U) SLUS-12345 DEADBEEF

[60 FPS]
author=YourName
description=Unlocks the framerate to 60fps. May need EE Overclock.
patch=0,EE,00000000,word,00000000

[No-Interlacing]
author=YourName
description=Disables interlaced rendering for a stable image.
gsinterlacemode=1
patch=1,EE,00000000,word,00000000

[Remove Blur]
author=YourName
description=Removes the blur/ghosting filter.
patch=1,EE,00000000,word,00000000
